<title>JAPAN: MOODY'S ASSIGNS A2 TO JAPAN REAL ESTATE INV BONDS.</title>
<headline>MOODY'S ASSIGNS A2 TO JAPAN REAL ESTATE INV BONDS.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Moody's Investors Service said on Friday that it has assigned an A2 rating to eight billion yen worth of secured zero coupon bonds due 2002 issued by Japan Real Estate Investment Company No.1 (JRIC No.1).</p>
<p>The funds raised through the bonds will be used to purchase properties which have been used as collateral for non-performing loans at the Bank of Yokohama Ltd.</p>
<p>JRIC is a special purpose company established in the Cayman Islands.</p>
</text>
